  "description": "Teach your reader something true!",
  "video": {
    "youtubeId": "DN4d76QP_MA",
    "title": "Informational Writing for Kids — What Is It?",
    "channel": "Teaching Without Frills"
  },
  "steps": [
    "Informational writing teaches the reader about something TRUE — it uses facts, not make-believe.",
    "A fact is something real you can check: 'Hummingbirds can fly backwards.' An opinion is what someone thinks: 'Hummingbirds are pretty.'",
    "Start with a topic sentence, add fact details, then a closing sentence.",
    "Example topic: 'The Doctor Bird' — facts: it lives only in Jamaica, it is our national bird, it has long tail feathers!"
  ],
